Connecting Grafana to Data Sources
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure Prometheus as a time-series monitoring system
Install and configure InfluxDB as a time-series database
Connect Grafana to both Prometheus and InfluxDB data sources
Test and verify data source connections in Grafana
Understand the differences between various data source types
Configure basic data queries from multiple sources
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic knowledge of Linux command line operations
Understanding of fundamental networking concepts (ports, localhost)
Familiarity with text editors like nano or vim
Basic understanding of databases and monitoring concepts
Completion of previous Grafana installation labs (or equivalent knowledge)
